tions across RAG domains, semantic\nsearch using vector embeddings, knowledge graph construction,\nNMF, and legal information systems.\n2.1 Non-Negative Matrix Factorization for\nPattern Discovery\nNMF is a dimensionality reduction technique used to uncover latent\npatterns in data. [ 33] analyzed NMF as an interpretable method\nfor extracting features and topics from large datasets, specifically\nhighlighting its ability to identify meaningful and non-overlapping\ncomponents. Building on this work, [ 27] introduced sparseness\nconstraints for better", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 1926, "end_char_idx": 3027, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "d4929d92-d903-4688-b4e9-f15a035eb15e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "5c080e3b45971b1577cfaa9f8d34477d0a741a3af7b30680a69c739237ddb152", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "dcf68a07-445b-4acc-b830-d2168aa5fea2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "cde671a4bf3ce522b4c09e48cc584a659b9c0b533c98655587d51414c2046952", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "84f13d7a-dc4c-489b-a186-6ab13dc5a7a6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "a5253f4499e61c7113c786982490cef6e86c24bb45530c0b3fed83c5ef6a52a1", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "on this work, [ 27] introduced sparseness\nconstraints for better interpretability, improving applications of\nNMF in real-world scenarios through more focused feature selec-\ntion. In the legal domain, NMF has been valuable for analyzingcomplex textual data, such as case law and statutes, and assist-\ning with topic discovery and clustering. For instance, [14] applied\nNMF to legal documents to extract latent topics and visualize rela-\ntionships, demonstrating how NMF\u2019s interpretable structure aids\nresearchers in identifying underlying topics not readily apparent in\nraw text. They even applied NMF hierarchically to find fine-grained\ntopics, however did not have a way to approximate the number\nof clusters automatically at each decomposition. More recently,\n[35] proposed a guided semi-supervised NMF approach for topic\ndiscovery in legal documents, using domain knowledge to steer\nfactorization and ensure the extracted topics remain highly rele-\nvant. This semi-supervised extension bridges the gap between fully\nautomated unsupervised techniques and", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 2963, "end_char_idx": 4019, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "84f13d7a-dc4c-489b-a186-6ab13dc5a7a6", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "5c080e3b45971b1577cfaa9f8d34477d0a741a3af7b30680a69c739237ddb152", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "d4929d92-d903-4688-b4e9-f15a035eb15e", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "434bc0a0cad30cdc30128791fe9fc5503abf480045830dea3091206f38823c32", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "e1424a1a-ce07-4131-b01c-405c9f91913c", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "8c9887651dc441a20ef2624f4884bbe6da224038cb6e4a860f67a9f4a32c4da6", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "extension bridges the gap between fully\nautomated unsupervised techniques and expert-driven analysis.\nNMF\u2019s utility in legal contexts is particularly significant, providing\nan interpretable framework for analyzing large textual datasets.\n2.2 Retrieval-Augmented Generation\nRAG has emerged as a foundational approach for improving AI sys-\ntems across various domains, including law. For instance, [ 34] intro-\nduced a framework that dynamically retrieves relevant documents\nto ground generative outputs, achieving notable gains in accuracy.\nBuilding on this idea, [ 26] proposed a retrieval-augmented pre-\ntraining method that integrates external knowledge for improved\ndownstream task performance. In contrast, [ 29] demonstrated the\neffectiveness of retrieval in open-domain question answering. These\nadvances lay the groundwork for applying RAG to the legal sector,\nwhere the method\u2019s ability to ground LLMs in authoritative texts\nreduces hallucinations and increases accuracy in tasks such as case\nlaw retrieval, statutory reasoning, and judgment prediction. Notable\nexamples include CBR-RAG,", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 3942, "end_char_idx": 5037, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "e1424a1a-ce07-4131-b01c-405c9f91913c", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "5c080e3b45971b1577cfaa9f8d34477d0a741a3af7b30680a69c739237ddb152", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "84f13d7a-dc4c-489b-a186-6ab13dc5a7a6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "13b845642d9c6ba751e64235619818d5fa753dfd8760262bb35e3a7a9f535dec", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "62592fb2-d6d1-4ed4-9274-6601640a3af2", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "45b76814708cc34ecbdbea8e9d2b4a0c60cd5562f03756786435f47996ee0dc9", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "reasoning, and judgment prediction. Notable\nexamples include CBR-RAG, which incorporates Case-Based Rea-\nsoning to structure retrieval for legal QA [ 51], and LegalBench-RAG.\nThis benchmark suite tailors evaluation metrics to the demands of\nlegal information synthesis [ 42]. Parallel work has demonstrated\nRAG\u2019s capabilities in other domains, such as malware data analysis,\nby combining embeddings, KGs, and NMF [ 9]. Other works show\nhow LLMs can dynamically decide when and what to retrieve to\nimprove legal reasoning [ 32] and how multi-step legal judgment\nprediction can benefit from iterative retrieval and generation [ 48],\nfurther demonstrating th effectiveness of combining retrieval strate-\ngies with LLMs.\n2.3 Semantic Search with Vector Embeddings\nSemantic search operates on dense vector representations to find\nthe deeper semantic relationships in texts, going beyond keyword\nmatching to proper context retrieval [ 26,31]. This search is espe-\ncially valuable in the legal domain, where queries often demand", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 4968, "end_char_idx": 5989, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "62592fb2-d6d1-4ed4-9274-6601640a3af2", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_1", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "5c080e3b45971b1577cfaa9f8d34477d0a741a3af7b30680a69c739237ddb152", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "e1424a1a-ce07-4131-b01c-405c9f91913c", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "2", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "18b0bc1b43d89b5be86ead1d91b0353e970af33e0856ba9bc71415619a649d4c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "is espe-\ncially valuable in the legal domain, where queries often demand con-\nceptual rather than surface-level understanding. Domain-specific\npretraining has become increasingly important, as in LEGAL-BERT\n[17], outperforming general-purpose models by better capturing\nlegal language nuances. Benchmarks like LeCaRD [ 36] show the\neffectiveness of dense retrievers\u2014such as SBERT\u2014in legal case re-\ntrieval of Chinese law and the abilities of hybrid approaches that\nintegrate both lexical and dense retrieval methods. Hierarchical\ntransformer architectures [ 28] and long-context models like Long-\nformer [ 10] further address the challenges of lengthy legal docu-\nments. In contrast, citation-driven approaches such as SPECTER", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 5917, "end_char_idx": 6643, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "1452ab98-aae7-421a-bfa3-ab95185904a7", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_2", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "57b60539ff493a285ea808d38b5c69b89fd129eb085f15ea204362f5bea0f6a4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ca5454c8-fa00-485b-80bb-f78ab429a2fa", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "2dd5438a8daf777a9f20f56030b3d67f62be03b8180feb447079c784e6a0a356", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "Bridging Legal Knowledge and AI:\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation with Vector Stores, Knowledge Graphs, and Hierarchical Non-negative Matrix Factorization ICAIL 2025, June 16\u201320, 2024, Chicago, IL, USA\n[20] leverage metadata to improve retrieval. Furthermore, work on\nneighborhood contrastive learning for scientific document represen-\ntations (SciNCL) [ 41] demonstrates how controlled nearest neighbor\nsampling over citation graph embeddings can provide continuous\nsimilarity. This strategy could also inform citation-based retrieval\nimprovements in legal domains. Challenges remain around scaling,\nexplainability, and incorporating heterogeneous data sources in\nreal-world legal workflows.\n2.4 Knowledge Graphs in Legal Research\nIn the legal domain, researchers have used KGs for knowledge ex-\ntraction [ 46], constructed domain-specific graphs tailored to legal\ncontexts [ 23], and explored their potential for addressing trust, pri-\nvacy, and transparency concerns [ 15]. Recent studies have demon-\nstrated the effectiveness of", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 1030, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "ca5454c8-fa00-485b-80bb-f78ab429a2fa", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-0