a-\npacity to represent intricate legal concepts, structure regulatory\nframeworks, and encourage reasoning over legal data.\n2.5 Legal Systems and Case Retrieval\nLegal information systems have evolved rapidly with the advent of\nneural architectures and hybrid retrieval pipelines, enabling precise\ntasks such as precedent retrieval, statute matching, and judgment\nprediction [ 16,19,45]. Benchmarks like LeCaRD [ 36] and LexGLUE\n[18], along with LEGAL-BERT-based systems [ 17], have demon-\nstrated the capability of these neural methods to improve accuracy\nin analyzing", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 946, "end_char_idx": 1957, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "8b3a7792-42d2-4eb6-a352-b07fc0c5b5fa", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_2", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "57b60539ff493a285ea808d38b5c69b89fd129eb085f15ea204362f5bea0f6a4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "ca5454c8-fa00-485b-80bb-f78ab429a2fa", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "30a1c1fee1a2a8dc6248ddbafb4a6eb2a9b8cd62b2e83e80c6187468797167f4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "8fc2d81f-5777-4261-9b76-49d8a3852601", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "56164df191f0d38614989ac811b63a6d0eb4dbb08828824817aff5fec7d728c4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "demon-\nstrated the capability of these neural methods to improve accuracy\nin analyzing legal corpora. In particular, researchers have leveraged\nstructured reasoning with transformers and graph representations\nto link statutes and precedents, as evidenced in the COLIEE competi-\ntion [ 43]. Nonetheless, several limitations remain: data scarcity and\njurisdictional bias continue to restrict the generalizability of such\nmodels. At the same time, resource-intensive retrievers like BERT-\nbased cross-encoders [ 53] have challenges scaling to large-scale\nlegal databases. Earlier works in juris-informatics have highlighted\nthe potential of automating legal reasoning and document analysis\n[8], laying the groundwork for modern approaches that fuse knowl-\nedge graphs, transformers, vector stores, and agent-oriented RAG\npipelines to deliver more explainable and efficient legal research\nworkflows.\n3 METHODS\nLaws and their interpretations are limited in application to their\nrespective jurisdictions. This work selected the State of New Mexico,\nusing the available Supreme Court and Court of", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 1871, "end_char_idx": 2960, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "8fc2d81f-5777-4261-9b76-49d8a3852601", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_2", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "57b60539ff493a285ea808d38b5c69b89fd129eb085f15ea204362f5bea0f6a4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "8b3a7792-42d2-4eb6-a352-b07fc0c5b5fa", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "3c42723f0ce55b9a6c3ed5390ff63ea93c5f91eb40bf010ca3118c12b443897e", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "f4193b7b-538e-43e3-9108-2a9bc224b968", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "e22032d98d8ee8e1a93eb705a58357916ae04b4f5322685fbebe524b04f7375a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "work selected the State of New Mexico,\nusing the available Supreme Court and Court of Appeals case law,\nthe state constitution, and state statutes as the main data resource.\n3.1 Data Collection\nTo compile a research-oriented corpus of legal documents, we uti-\nlized Justia\u2019s publicly accessible resources, in full compliance with\ntheir Terms of Service and any applicable usage guidelines, includ-\ning robots.txt. We developed a restricted andresponsible crawler to\nonly access permitted documents\u2014namely statutes, constitutionalprovisions, and case law in the public domain\u2014and to avoid any\nsections or usage not authorized by Justia\u2019s policies. To minimize\nserver load and respect rate limits, our scraper introduces time\ndelays between requests, monitors for HTTP status codes indicat-\ning rate-limiting or errors, and uses exponential backoff to handle\npotential network disruptions gracefully.\nFrom the main landing page, a dynamic crawler identifies only\nthose hyperlinks consistent with the site\u2019s navigation structure and\nrelevant public legal content, converting them to absolute URLs\nand recursively traversing", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 2875, "end_char_idx": 3995, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "f4193b7b-538e-43e3-9108-2a9bc224b968", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_2", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "57b60539ff493a285ea808d38b5c69b89fd129eb085f15ea204362f5bea0f6a4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "8fc2d81f-5777-4261-9b76-49d8a3852601", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "d7af8d19a5ad031ecf3a021a03d6eb9533161405949a65e98d836ed251d51e69", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "c76132d5-778b-40d6-867b-28a57d0d9cb6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "46d144b92c1e3a63d329102e3919e2f536e53d09d03a516a33452abedad00244", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "public legal content, converting them to absolute URLs\nand recursively traversing nested content where permitted. Our\nprocess extracts metadata such as chapter names, article titles,\nsection numbers, full text for statutes, constitutional provisions, and\njudicial opinions for New Mexico\u2019s Court of Appeals and Supreme\nCourt cases.\nThroughout this procedure, we take multiple measures to main-\ntain compliance and transparency:\n\u2022Logs track processed URLs to prevent duplication, resume\ninterrupted crawls responsibly, and record request timing.\n\u2022Rate-limiting measures ensure we do not exceed usage\nthresholds or impose an undue burden on Justia\u2019s servers.\n\u2022No circumvention of technical safeguards defined in\nrobots.txt and the TOS restrictions.\n\u2022Non-commercial use only : we do not republish, sell, or\notherwise exploit Justia\u2019s content and only use it for legiti-\nmate scholarly research.\nThese practices keep the data process ethical, legally sound, and\nconsistent with Justia\u2019s rules for site usage and content retrieval.\n3.2 Dimension Reduction in Legal Texts\nLegal documents-", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 3914, "end_char_idx": 4996, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "c76132d5-778b-40d6-867b-28a57d0d9cb6", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_2", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "57b60539ff493a285ea808d38b5c69b89fd129eb085f15ea204362f5bea0f6a4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "f4193b7b-538e-43e3-9108-2a9bc224b968", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "1e4e2a744fac937979ee21111eb20d9f131c3761f4a1677af431cc46a7eb4263", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "27899468-7920-4971-aa11-a394cadf7ab4", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "09c7340071ce140dfb3e3c28a8db471367e93763b181d60667810a97a19970d0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "content retrieval.\n3.2 Dimension Reduction in Legal Texts\nLegal documents- constitutions, statutes, and case law- are tradi-\ntionally organized into chapters, articles, and sections, but these\nstructures do not always match the latent patterns revealed through\nfactorization. Each document type is analyzed separately using non-\nnegative tensor and matrix factorization to explore these hidden\nrelationships. A TF-IDF matrix, X, is first constructed from the\ncleaned corpus. Constitutional provisions, statutory clauses, and\ncase law paragraphs form the units of analysis for clustering.\nIn this study, we use the public repository called Tensor Extrac-\ntion of Latent Features (T-ELF )1[24], combined with automatic\nmodel selection, to decompose Xinto coherent topic H-clusters.\nT-ELF efficiently identifies latent topics, grouping constitutional\nprovisions around themes such as \u201cseparation of powers\u201d and clus-\ntering statutes and case law based on regulatory objectives and\nrecurring legal doctrines, respectively.\n3.2.1 Application of", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 4922, "end_char_idx": 5961, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "27899468-7920-4971-aa11-a394cadf7ab4", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_2", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "57b60539ff493a285ea808d38b5c69b89fd129eb085f15ea204362f5bea0f6a4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "c76132d5-778b-40d6-867b-28a57d0d9cb6", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "3", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "9d0ee817d9b733dccde3d86ab0292fd3eafa0c98bd3218e571f0ed15c25a6b63", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "and\nrecurring legal doctrines, respectively.\n3.2.1 Application of Non-Negative Matrix Factorization to Legal\nTexts. NMF approximates the matrix Xwith two non-negative ma-\ntrices, WandH:\nX\u2248W\u00b7H,\nwhere Wdescribes how terms distribute over topics, and H\ndescribes how these topics distribute across documents. Constitu-\ntional articles and sections reveal underlying governance or civil\nrights themes; statute clauses highlight regulatory objectives, and\n1https://github.com/lanl/T-ELF", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 5896, "end_char_idx": 6377, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "c2c7e760-cbb4-4713-9d81-f0e88176ec5b", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_3", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "6520389803fea9e5f6962be330881974d9748b7a949d572ee20b0e9d81082099", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "d9bce701-b9d0-4eb8-87cf-c356be75fec0", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "e24cee0acba2dc2ab897c592ae468a1d51eaf33384d6e7feaff5af4ed1a3c08b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "ICAIL 2025, June 16\u201320, 2024, Chicago, IL, USA Barron et al.\nsegmented judicial opinions expose common doctrines and legal\nreasoning patterns.\n3.2.2 Automatic Model Determination Using NMFk. A central chal-\nlenge in applying NMF is selecting the best number of latent fea-\ntures ( \ud835\udc58). We use NMFk [7], which combines clustering stability with\nreconstruction accuracy. Bootstrap resampling generates slightly\nperturbed versions of the original matrix, and repeated decompo-\nsitions measure how consistently clusters form. Silhouette scores\nhelp ensure cohesive, well-separated topics, while reconstruction\nerror verifies that the model effectively captures patterns in the\noriginal data.\nBy adapting this NMF approach to a hierarchical setting, legal\ntexts can be organized into a tree-like structure. Constitutions may\nbe segmented into articles and sections, statutes into chapters and\nclauses, and case law into layered precedents and sub-issues. This\nhierarchical perspective enhances the", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 991, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "d9bce701-b9d0-4eb8-87cf-c356be75fec0", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_3", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "6520389803fea9e5f6962be330881974d9748b7a949d572ee20b0e9d81082099", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "c2c7e760-cbb4-4713-9d81-f0e88176ec5b", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "d2db22b0848f4e3f9cab26260b181d77f5e20f13b5332db47631ef3f69a5f91b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "dbb5d155-fa23-4936-b9fb-c0f8c87f759c", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "149a631db20801a34571ed2260073b1d38033321681a3a52f46475d356fb5a2c", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "into layered precedents and sub-issues. This\nhierarchical perspective enhances the discovery of latent relation-\nships at multiple levels of granularity, facilitating deeper analyses\nof large-scale legal corpora.\nStatute\nSection\n[Citation]Constitution\nSection\n[Citation]Supreme  \nCourt  \nCase Law\n[Year]Appeals\nCourt  \nCase Law\n[Year]\nNMFk  \nTopic\n[Label,  \nDocument Count]NMFk\nKeywordBOW\nVocabulary\nFigure 1: Knowledge Graph Schema, with the primary iden-\ntifier in bold and attributes in brackets.\n3.3 Knowledge Graph\nFeatures derived from T-ELF and document metadata are trans-\nformed into a series of head, entity, and tail relations, forming\ndirectional triplets integrated into a Neo4j KG [37].\nIn the legal context, the KG incorporates metadata and latent\nfeatures extracted from constitutions, statutes, and case law. The\nprimary nodes in the graph represent legal documents, including\nconstitutional", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 909, "end_char_idx": 1817, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "dbb5d155-fa23-4936-b9fb-c0f8c87f759c", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_3", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "6520389803fea9e5f6962be330881974d9748b7a949d572ee20b0e9d81082099", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "d9bce701-b9d0-4eb8-87cf-c356be75fec0", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "d8c6cbf2e81d826e56e1a11bdccfc30dcb3679104c076675925ab6f78479c5ec", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "7be70dea-4fc2-43e2-b0b0-617caf095d34", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "5c60701e4efee988296efc3df3fe94971f6bd248ef27601e33a7db5155f8a1d3", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "law. The\nprimary nodes in the graph represent legal documents, including\nconstitutional provisions, statutory sections, and judicial opinions.\nThese nodes are enriched with metadata such as titles, hierarchical\nidentifiers (e.g., chapter and section numbers), jurisdiction, court\nnames, decision dates, and topics derived from latent features.\nEdges in the KG establish relationships between nodes to repre-\nsent the interconnected nature of legal documents. For instance:\n\u2022Constitutional Nodes: Linked to statutory provisions or\njudicial interpretations that reference or rely on specific\nconstitutional clauses.\n\u2022Statutory Nodes: Connected to cases interpreting the statute\nor related provisions within the same legislative framework.\n\u2022Case Law Nodes: Interlinked based on shared topics, com-\nmon legal principles, or hierarchical relationships in appel-\nlate decisions.This graph structure enables the RAG system to query and re-\ntrieve legal documents based on semantic similarity and explicit\nrelationships. For example, a query about \"due process\" might re-\ntrieve the relevant constitutional clause, cases that discuss its inter-\npretation, and statutory provisions impacted", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 1730, "end_char_idx": 2911, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "7be70dea-4fc2-43e2-b0b0-617caf095d34", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": ["file_name", "file_type", "file_size", "creation_date", "last_modified_date", "last_accessed_date"], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf_part_3", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "6520389803fea9e5f6962be330881974d9748b7a949d572ee20b0e9d81082099", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "2": {"node_id": "dbb5d155-fa23-4936-b9fb-c0f8c87f759c", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"page_label": "4", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "8658bd14550e1dd932cb446e0889696c622794ad9e6ad385fa41d221cc7005b5", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "2ae7bc10-83e5-40f6-aa96-daf4e455b94a", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "0acb2a0887c60f12d44305028726925fbc6e72e3929be10251281f427530f804", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "constitutional clause, cases that discuss its inter-\npretation, and statutory provisions impacted by those rulings. By\ncombining metadata and latent features, the KG supports advanced\nreasoning and logical traversal, enhancing the precision and depth\nof legal information retrieval.\nEach part had decomposition topics containing keywords that\nconnected to the documents. The bag of words (BOW) vocabulary\nwas also extracted and inserted into the knowledge graph. These\ncan be observed in the knowledge graph schema of Figure 1.\n3.4 Vector Store\nA vector database was implemented to manage and index legal doc-\numents, improving the RAG process for legal research. Using Mil-\nvus [ 47], the system stores vectorized representations of constitu-\ntions, statutes, and case law, treating each document type uniquely\nto ensure contextually relevant retrieval.\nConstitutional provisions are segmented into paragraphs, each\nassigned a unique ID, and vectorized using OpenAI\u2019s text-embeddin