: "C:\\Users\\anteb\\PycharmProjects\\JupyterProject\\naive_rag\\data\\raw\\2502.20364.pdf", "file_type": "application/pdf", "file_size": 6884424, "creation_date": "2025-03-04", "last_modified_date": "2025-03-03"}, "hash": "75b1fde59461b64ac2a6a259713af89413885841ca3b272b995ec40cf8f11e2b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "ddf5e78a-98fd-40ac-8282-c4c9001c3f62", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "4a9a381db541ee297f72cf387d50ae3a90b3ae89b47bd9c542cde19285d7fc47", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "again placed into a single dataset but chunked\nat 3000 characters with 500 overlapping. The top row, with more\nconcise and structured concepts, decreased slightly in performance,\nwhereas the cases significantly improved. This is likely because the\nconcepts are broken down across multiple texts instead of being in\none coherent text to query. Still, with the decrease, the structured\ntexts outperformed the cases by more than 20%. Third, the NMFk\nhierarchical cases are incorporated into the vector store process,\nwhere each topic has an individual vector store. The topics per\nquery were controlled such that the query was searched in the vec-\ntor store corresponding to the question origin. Topic identification\nin the vector store is an outstanding problem for future work. When\ntheNMFk hierarchical topics were introduced, the performancesignificantly improved across all data sources, with the most sig-\nnificant gains in the longer case texts. When the chunking process\nwas incrementally added on top of the NMFk topics, the cases", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 2129, "end_char_idx": 3165, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "ddf5e78a-98fd-40ac-8282-c4c9001c3f62", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"page_label": "8", "file_name": "2502.20364.pdf", "file_path": "C:\\Users\\anteb\\Pych